e central museum of fine arts in Ajaccio on Corsica. Located within the gated Palais Fesch, it is in the town's Borgu d'Ajaccio quarter. It was established by Napoleon I's uncle, cardinal Joseph Fesch (a Prince of France from 1807), in Fesch's birthplace.","wpu":"Musée Fesch","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ajaccio-Palais_Fesch.jpg/960px-Ajaccio-Palais_Fesch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palais Lantivy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.919444,"lo":8.736389,"d":495,"ds":"Palais Lantivy is a Neoclassical palace in Ajaccio, Corsica. It serves as the Corsican Prefecture, the headquarters for administration of the department of Corse-du-Sud and the General Council. Construction occurred between 1826 and 1830, under a plan of the architect Alphonse de Gisors.","wpu":"Palais Lantivy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/H%C3%B4tel_de_pr%C3%A9fecture_de_Corse-du-Sud.jpg/960px-H%C3%B4tel_de_pr%C3%A9fecture_de_Corse-du-Sud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Citadelle d'Ajaccio","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.916667,"lo":8.740278,"d":704,"ds":"Citadelle d'Ajaccio is a fortress in Corse-du-Sud, France. It was built in 1492.","wpu":"Citadelle d'Ajaccio","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Ajaccio_citadelle_echauguette.jpg/960px-Ajaccio_citadelle_echauguette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Ajaccio","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.916389,"lo":8.729722,"d":1124,"ds":"The Diocese of Ajaccio (Latin: Dioecesis Adiacensis; French: Diocèse d'Ajaccio) is a Latin Church ecclesiastical jurisdiction or diocese of the Catholic Church in France. The diocese comprises the whole of the island of Corsica. Erected in the 3rd century, the diocese was formerly a suffragan of the Archdiocese of Pisa.","wpu":"Diocese of Ajaccio","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Eglise_Ajaccio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Liamone","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.93,"lo":8.73,"d":1135,"ds":"Liamone was a department of the French island of Corsica between 1793 and 1811. It was located in the southern and western parts of the island, and its capital was Ajaccio. Liamone was created in 1793 by the division of the former department of Corse, which covered the whole island.","wpu":"Liamone","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Departements_of_French_Empire_South_1811-fr.svg/960px-Departements_of_French_Empire_South_1811-fr.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gravona","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.904722,"lo":8.798333,"d":5237,"ds":"The Gravona is a river on the island of Corsica, France. It flows from the center of the island southwest to the Gulf of Ajaccio. Its entire course is in the Corse-du-Sud Department of France.","wpu":"Gravona","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Gravona2.JPG/960px-Gravona2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tour de Capitello","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.904167,"lo":8.799167,"d":5324,"ds":"The Tour de Capitello (Corsican: Torra di Capiteddu) is a Genoese tower located in the commune of Grosseto-Prugna (Corse-du-Sud) on the coast of the French island of Corsica. The tower lies to the south of Ajaccio near the Porticcio beach. The construction of the tower was begun in 1552.","wpu":"Tour de Capitello","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Torra_di_Capiteddu.JPG/960px-Torra_di_Capiteddu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Alata, Corse-du-Sud","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.9778,"lo":8.7439,"d":6102,"ds":"Alata (French pronunciation: [alata]) is a commune in the Corse-du-Sud department, on the French island of Corsica. It is within the metropolitan area of the capital Ajaccio.","wpu":"Alata, Corse-du-Sud","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Alata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Afa, Corse-du-Sud","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.9847,"lo":8.7964,"d":8295,"ds":"Afa (French pronunciation: [afa]), Italian: Afà (Italian pronunciation: [a'fa]), Corsican: Afà, is a commune in the Corse-du-Sud department on the island and collectivity of Corsica, France.","wpu":"Afa, Corse-du-Sud","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Afa_Kirche.jpg/960px-Afa_Kirche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Torra di l'Isuledda","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.844444,"lo":8.754722,"d":8819,"ds":"The Tower of Isuledda (Corsican: Torra di l'Isuledda) is a Genoese tower located in the commune of Pietrosella (Corse-du-Sud) on the Corsica. The tower sits at an elevation of 68 m on a promontory, the Punta di Sette Nave, which forms the southern limit of the Gulf of Ajaccio. The tower was built in around 1597.","wpu":"Torra di l'Isuledda","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Tour_de_l%27isolella.JPG/960px-Tour_de_l%27isolella.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ajaccio is the capital and largest city of Corsica, France. It forms a French commune, prefecture of the department of Corse-du-Sud, and head office of the Collectivité territoriale de Corse (capital city of Corsica). It is also the largest settlement on the island.","wpu":"Ajaccio","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Port_Tino_Rossi_-_Ajaccio_%2815148706455%29.jpg/960px-Port_Tino_Rossi_-_Ajaccio_%2815148706455%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}